  <iati-identifier>GB-GOV-1-301049-105</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="GB-GOV-1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UK - Foreign, Commonwealth Development Office (FCDO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">[Capital] Funding Support to Science Granting Councils, promote gender equality and support monitoring and evaluation.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Science Granting Councils Initiative in sub-Saharan Africa (SGCI 1) from 2015 &#x2013; 2020, was a  partnership between FCDO, the Canadian International Development Research Centre (IDRC) and South Africa&#x2019;s National Research Foundation (NRF). Phase 1 of SGCI improved the delivery and 
management of research funds by Science granting councils (SGCs) and facilitated new collaborative research partnerships between African governments. Investment in a second phase of the programme (2021 to 2025), will enable SGCI 2 to: 

1) Support and guide the setting up of new councils though consultation on best practice and policy mechanisms in priority countries for the UK (Nigeria and Sierra Leone). 

2) Provide a separate UK only platform for the UK to strengthen bi-lateral research partnerships and science diplomacy and respond to the new framework for international science partnerships as set out in the IR. 

3) Provide research funding to address national priorities in partner countries and build capacity through a &#x2018;learning by doing&#x2019; approach, while simultaneous supporting research in developing countries which addresses the SDGs. 

4) Expand work on gender and inclusion, which was identified as a priority area in SGCI 1 and is essential to ensure the STEM aspirations of women and girls is obtainable. 

5) Drive coherence xHMG and leverage additional research funding xHMG.</narrative>
  </description>
